Carafe: the Horizon server keeps window hooks: set_hook, remove_hook, start_hook_chain, finish_hook_chain and
get_hook_info work for the hooks a program sets on its own threads, and every thread's shared queue data counts
the hooks that run in it, so win32u calls them. Programs built on MFC hook window creation with WH_CBT before
their first window and stop with CMemoryException when the hook is refused. Low-level, journal and win event
hooks are still refused.
LGPL-2.1-or-later, as the file it changes.

